{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/WBNS10TV/posts/fox-news-currently-airs-in-canada-and-it-wasnt-banned-in-the-uk-instead-the-netw/10160675320879369/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/WBNS10TV/posts/fox-news-currently-airs-in-canada-and-it-wasnt-banned-in-the-uk-instead-the-netw/10160675320879369/","title":"10TV - WBNS","description":"Fox News currently airs in Canada, and it wasn’t banned in the U.K. Instead, the network decided to stop broadcasting there in 2017 because of low viewership.","language":"en","text":"Fox News currently airs in Canada, and it wasn’t banned in the U.K. Instead, the network decided to stop broadcasting there in 2017 because of low viewership.\n\nAll reactions:\n\n57 comments\n\n3 shares\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nBobby Humphrey\n\nIs nothing but lies\n\nDuke Moody\n\nThe UK went from having an empire across the globe to just ruling their little island. They would never understand any policy that isn't woke.\n\n1\n\nView all 2 replies\n\nFred McNutt\n\nPer Nielsen Data…….\n\nFox News was the most watched cable news channel in America for the sixth consecutive year in 2021.\n\nFox averaged 1.3 million in total day viewers this year, compared to 919,000 at MSNBC and 787,000 watching CNN. In prime time, Fox averaged 2.3 million viewers, including an average of 374,000 within the industry's coveted 25- to 54-year-old demographic.\n\nNielsen data shows that Fox held 44 percent of the cable news audience in total day viewership and 47 percent of audience share in total viewers in prime time in 2021, an increase from last year.\n\nFox's top-rated program, \"Tucker Carlson Tonight,\" averaged 3.1 million viewers a night this year. Sean Hannity's program, the network's second highest-rated, averaged 2.8 million.\n\n4\n\nView all 16 replies\n\nArielle Lucius\n\nUk is smarter than USA then. Never believe a word I hear on fox\n\n34\n\nView all 5 replies\n\nBrad Park\n\nFox is like 'The Onion' except people know The Onion is Fake.\n\n24\n\nView all 13 replies\n\nRandy Lee\n\nThey really shouldn't be allowed to refer to themselves as \"news\" considering any time they get sued their first defense is that they're simply entertainment and playing a character, not meant to be taken seriously.\n\n11\n\nView 1 reply\n\nSteven C Brogan\n\nIt’s funny how people trash fox, but cnn is the one always getting sued and losing!\n\nMost relevant is selected, so some comments may have been filtered out.","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2027.2836740041384,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}